d 'ATIP_SCORE': module to score outliers on two separate axes (evidence and magnitude)
d
d  atip_score generalizes atip_reglas (calls it internally):
d instead of a single binary flag, it produces two continuous axes
d -- N_REGLAS (how many of the 5 rules fired, 0-5) and
d MAGNITUD_LOCAL (|z|, how far the value is) -- kept separate so
d that a case with strong evidence but modest magnitude can be
d distinguished from one with both, following the selective editing
d framework of de Waal, Pannekoek and Scholtus (2011, Handbook of
d Statistical Data Editing and Imputation, Wiley). 
d
d KW: outliers
d KW: score
d
d Requires: Stata version 14 and atip_reglas from SSC (q.v.)
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260802
d
d Author: Andres Talavera Cuya,   Direccion Nacional de Censos y Encuestas -- INEI Peru
d Support: email talaveracuya@@gmail.com
d
f atip_score.ado
f atip_score.sthlp
